WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.768
House Republicans venting their anger

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.169
to the leader of the second largest

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.971
teacher's union in the country.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:05.672
On Capitol Hill

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.840
this week, Republicans

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.440
allege that

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.808
the union and others

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.209
worked

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:09.943
with the CDC

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.810
to keep schools

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.045
closed longer

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.314
than necessary amid the COVID pandemic.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.717
But did HFT ever provide

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.986
suggested revisions to the CDC's

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.088
operational strategy regarding school

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.857
closures or reopenings?

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.824
Did you

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.760
suggest revisions

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.461
to their operational strategy?

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.464
What we suggested, sir, was ideas.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.633
I'm a member of Congress

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.035
that sits on two committees

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.337
that deal with this, the CDC.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.773
I don't have a direct number

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.408
to Director Walensky.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.308
Do you

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:50.650
I do not talk to represent.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.785
You have the gov

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.820
you have a direct number to to.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.921
Director Walensky,

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.157
do I have Director William Ski's direct?

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.358
No. Yes. Yes.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.626
I have director of Wetlands,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.627
his direct number.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.361
Well, hopefully

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.896
she'll give it to me, too.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.931
So I've been to some weird hearings

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.966
in this Congress, Mr.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:07.333
Chairman,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.035
but this one might be the weirdest

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.070
because it's

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.271
convened in order

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.306
to accuse a federal agency

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.241
of the crime of consulting

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.543
with American citizens.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:18.611
Randi

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.779
Weingarten is the president

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.181
of the American Federation of Teachers,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:21.948
and she joins me now.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.483
Randi, great to have you here.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:23.817
Basically,

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.617
it sounds like what they were saying

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.952
was that you had undue

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.887
influence on the CDC

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.522
to make policy,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.357
I guess, about when schools would reopen.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.693
What's your response to that?

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.830
So, you know, we represent teachers

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.564
and nurses.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.765
We're actually the fastest

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.233
growing nurse union these days.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.336
And with the Biden administration

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.471
coming in,

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.206
they wanted to reopen schools

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.273
more fulsomely.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.842
We wanted to reopen schools

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.009
more fulsomely.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.412
And we said during the transition,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.481
you need to have clear

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.716
scientific based guidance

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.651
that people can understand.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.587
I mean, most of us are not scientists.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:04.057
So And and what we were getting for

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:04.457
the months

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.427
beforehand was unclear and unhelpful.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.662
So you needed the resources

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.096
for things

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.631
like ventilation

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.400
masks, the things that you know,

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.370
and in a respiratory disease

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.240
that's not seen, you could have

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.209
that would help people testing.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.446
And you needed clear guidance, Scott?

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:27.247
Yeah.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.549
We don't know each other,

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.551
but speaking on behalf of millions

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.786
of American parents, I have four at home.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.788
I had to teach him at home.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.191
My wife had to teach them at home.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.160
I am stunned at what you have said

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.060
this week

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:44.030
about your claiming to have

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.999
wanted to reopen schools.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.633
I think most

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:47.467
you'll find that

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.101
most parents

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.269
believe you were the tip

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.904
of the spear of school closures.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.739
There are numerous statements

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.475
you made over the summer of 20 scaring

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.710
people to death about the possibility

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.678
of opening schools.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:02:59.979
And I hear no remorse

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.582
whatsoever about the generational damage

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.050
that's been done to these.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.651
I have two kids

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.885
with learning differences.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.153
Do you know how hard it is for them

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.488
to learn at home

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.455
and not in a classroom

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.991
that was designed for them

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.458
and for you

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.127
to sit in front of Congress

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:16.629
and the American people and say,

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.299
Oh, I wanted to open them the whole time.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.733
I am shocked.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.901
I'm stunned.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:22.402
I'm stunned.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.204
And there are millions of parents

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.306
who feel the exact same way.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:28.208
Okay. Go ahead. Right. So

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:30.410
I don't

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.446
know you, sir, and you don't know me,

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.848
but I have worked for the last

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.750
20 or 30 years

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.186
helping kids every single day.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.222
I've been a school teacher.

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.557
I've been a union leader.

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.293
I knew

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.962
and understood the importance

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.730
of reopening schools

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.799
and the importance of making sure

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.334
that people were safe.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.501
And poll after poll

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.303
that we did have parents

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.372
and I spent a lot of time with parents,

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.342
said that they basically understood

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.777
and supported that we needed to do both

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:05.745
I'm really sorry.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.613
You think parents

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:07.780
wanted to keep the kids?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.449
Nobody wanted to parents.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.584
Nobody wanted to keep you in keeping in.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.052
Why did we fail?

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.520
How did Europe

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.189
and the rest of the civilized world

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.957
get this right? And we failed.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.225
They had the

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:19.692
how did they

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.028
how does that help the schools in Europe?

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.330
That opened sooner than we did

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.765
and most of them did.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.233
Had the mitigating circumstances,

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.801
had the mitigating strategies

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.303
that we were just talking about.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.805
And it wasn't negotiable.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:33.706
It wasn't.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.008
Oh, well,

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:37.110
it's inconvenient to have six feet

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.978
or it's inconvenient to have mass.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.813
They had these things.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.682
And the other thing they did,

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.284
and I don't know if was right or wrong,

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.251
the other thing they did

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.220
is they prioritized schools

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.488
over commerce.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.889
They prioritized schools

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.191
over bars and restaurants

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.192
and things like that.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:53.893
They did

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:54.861
Let me let me jump in

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.763
because I respect with Scott

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.530
saying obvious.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.064
I come at it

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.866
from a slightly different perspective,

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:00.933
having three children

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:03.303
also in public school in New York,

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.071
just outside of New York City.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.005
And we

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:06.873
we sort of dealt

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.808
with the cards that we were

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.809
we were handed.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:10.543
What I want to ask

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.812
you, Randi, is when you look back

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.681
and obviously we all know about hindsight

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:16.916
as a parent

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:17.250
on the

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.217
outside looking in

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.320
my sense of the situation was always

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.288
this is because the teachers

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.823
and the adults

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.158
around are

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:25.692
are more

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.593
afraid of this virus than the kids.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.829
Because as we found out fairly quickly,

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.031
we knew that children weren't going to be

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:35.068
that affected by this particular disease.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.202
And so from

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.270
from my perspective,

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.304
it seemed like

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.473
this was coming from the teachers

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.542
and the leadership on their side saying,

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.110
hey, this isn't safe for us.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:44.711
It's not safe

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:45.978
for our family members,

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.046
for the community.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.147
Is that what drove

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.149
you think, the decision to play it

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.050
extra safe

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.852
when it came to allowing the kids

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:54.253
to go back in the classroom?

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:54.487
Well,

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:55.855
I think the problem is

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:57.890
that teachers actually teach kids.

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:02.495
So if it wasn't if if I mean, look,

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:05.598
at what happened in Omaha from

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.334
when we were able because of testing,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.838
we're able to actually keep schools open

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.673
some schools shut

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.008
when there were too many teachers absent.

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:18.444
But we were able to keep schools open

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.780
because we understood and use testing

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.582
as a way to do that.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:25.118
So I think what happened was that

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.053
people were fearful.

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:29.188
You're absolutely right. But

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.992
even though thank God

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:36.028
kids didn't get as sick as adults,

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.464
adults were getting sick

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.233
and adults were dying.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:43.136
And so we were trying to figure out

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.171
and I'm not saying that.

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.672
Look, there were people

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:47.306
all across

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:50.610
America who were taking different

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.811
positions and,

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.813
you know, I was at the left,

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:55.448
including some of my members,

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:57.950
and you saw some of those things.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.453
But we were trying to figure out

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:03.222
what were the mitigating strategies

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:06.225
that were needed to keep schools open.

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:07.293
And that's

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:08.327
what you know,

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.830
and and that's what we tried to do.

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:13.232
From April 2020.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.034
And what I produced,

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:15.601
I went

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.170
and I testified in Congress

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.540
yesterday voluntarily, and I produced

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:23.576
much documentation

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:24.710
proving

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.280
all the things that we tried to say no.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:27.980
That's why

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:28.781
I keep on using

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.683
the form of administration

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.051
because frankly,

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.320
Governor Hogan, Governor Cuomo,

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:36.422
Rockefeller Foundation,

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.824
lots of governors,

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:38.691
they were working

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.526
in a really different way.

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:41.961
Than the Trump administration was.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:42.728
And the Trump

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.130
administration did a great job

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.932
in terms of vaccines,

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:48.301
but in terms of giving people

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:51.237
the kind of guidance to say

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:54.540
to do what Europe did, we didn't get it.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.142
And that's why in this

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.710
the investigative book

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.412
that just came out yesterday,

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:03.015
what they said was if we had gotten

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.383
that guidance,

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.285
that stockpile of guidance,

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.186
we would have been able

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.588
to open up earlier

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.323
and we just didn't get it, Randi.

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:11.390
Thank you very much.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.291
I'm thank you for answering

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:13.159
all of our questions.

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.694
We really appreciate you being here.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:14.994
You know,

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.662
the subject is not easy for a lot of

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:17.430
for everyone.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.366
But the bottom line is now

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:22.502
why are we not

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:24.570
doing everything we need to do now?

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.438
Yes, that has

00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:26.239
and that is

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:27.740
and that's what,

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.076
you know, I'd like to have seen

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.346
one question from the

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.849
Republicans that questioned me yesterday

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:39.318
for 3 hours about what we need to do.

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:40.353
Now, that's a great point.

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:40.820
And yes,

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.522
we do need to get ahead of this next one

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:43.589
and not just be reactive.

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:44.991
Thank you very much, guys.

